---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const waLink = `https://wa.me/${SITE.whatsapp}?text=${encodeURIComponent('Hi, I would like to contribute to Sudd Library: ')}`;
const mailLink = `mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Sudd Library')}`;
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="What Sudd Library is, who built it, and how it works.">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />

  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="about-hero-inner">
      <h1>Every South Sudanese learner deserves their own curriculum, free.</h1>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} puts lesson notes, schemes of work and past papers for the
        national curriculum in one search. No login. No cost. Works offline.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-body">
    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Many learners inside South Sudan, including displaced families, cannot easily
      reach materials for their own curriculum. {SITE.name} exists to close that gap.
      It is free to use, with no account and no data collected from you.
    </p>

    <h2>What you will find</h2>
    <p>
      Primary (P1 to P8), Secondary (S1 to S4) and AES, with lesson notes, schemes of
      work and past papers. Textbooks link directly to the National Curriculum
      Development Center (NCDC).
    </p>

    <h2>Is this official?</h2>
    <p>
      No. {SITE.name} follows the South Sudan national curriculum, but it is an
      independent project. It is not run by the NCDC or the Ministry of General
      Education and Instruction. Always use your official textbooks and your teacher's
      guidance together with these materials.
    </p>

    <h2>How the materials are made</h2>
    <p>
      Notes and schemes of work are prepared from the official NCDC textbooks and
      syllabus. AI tools help draft them, and each one is checked by a person before
      it is published. If you spot a mistake, please tell us and we will correct it.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Search by class, subject or topic, open a resource and download it. After the
      site has loaded once, it keeps working on a weak or missing connection. On your
      phone, use "Add to home screen" to open it like an app.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
    <p>
      I am {SITE.author}, a South Sudanese refugee living in {SITE.location}, and a
      computer science student. My own education was made possible by a sponsor, and
      I built {SITE.name} so that more learners can reach theirs. The code is open
      source on <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it free forever?</summary>
      <p>Yes. There are no fees, no accounts and no adverts.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I print and share the materials?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes, for teaching and learning. Please do not sell them. See the
        <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for the full terms.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it work without internet?</summary>
      <p>
        Pages you have already opened stay available offline. Open the ones you need
        while you have a connection.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can teachers contribute?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Send your notes or past papers through WhatsApp or email and they will
        be reviewed before being added.
      </p>
    </details>

    <h2>Contact and support</h2>
    <p>
      Teachers can share notes and past papers, and anyone can report a broken link
      or a mistake. <a href={waLink}>Message on WhatsApp</a> or
      <a href={mailLink}>send an email</a>. Every message gets read.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your school, organisation or sponsor would like to support this work,
      please get in touch using the same links.
    </p>

    <p class="about-small">
      See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for terms of use and how to
      request a takedown.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    background: var(--deep, #0F4788);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 30px 18px 28px;
  }
  .about-hero-inner {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .about-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 6vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .about-hero p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .about-body {
    padding: 8px 18px 40px;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .about-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 18px;
    margin: 24px 0 6px;
  }
  .about-body p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .about-body a { color: var(--deep-hover); text-decoration: underline; }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.3);
    padding: 10px 0;
  }
  summary {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  details p { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .about-small { margin-top: 26px; }
</style>
